614	    // ── Shutdown: write to QEMU isa-debug-exit port (0xf4).
615	    // Value 0x10 → QEMU exits with status 0.
616	    // On real hardware or without the device, falls through to HLT.
617	    sprintln!("[SHUTDOWN] μ∘δ=id. Goodbye.");
618	
619	    // `out` and `hlt` are privileged. On bare metal they are the QEMU
620	    // debug-exit device and the idle halt; in a userspace process they are a
621	    // general protection fault, which is what made the hosted build segfault on
622	    // quit. A host does not need a debug-exit device emulated at it -- it
623	    // exits.
624	    #[cfg(not(feature = "hosted"))]
